  <static seed="75" source="Library/TCNJ/TCNJ_MatrixLinearTransformation/problem16.pg">
    <statement><p>Let <m>T</m> be a one-to-one linear transformation from 
<m>{\mathbb R}^r</m> to
<m>{\mathbb R}^s</m>.</p>
<p><ol>
<li>
<p>What can one say about the relationship between
<m>r</m> and <m>s</m>.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<ol label="A.">
<li>
<p><m>r\geq s</m></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>r\lt s</m></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>r&gt;s</m></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>r\leq s</m></p>
</li>
<li>
<p>There is not enough information to tell</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</statement>
